cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Bounded Observer"
message: "If you use this work, please cite the capstone manuscript."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Murray
    given-names: Daniel John
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-1794-5945"
abstract: >-
  A research programme derived from one premise: an observer with finite access, standing inside
  the world it measures. Finite access forces a predictive state; bounded quantities force a
  composition law; that law forces a horizon; the horizon forces a hyperbolic geometry. The
  central theorem is the Universal Hyperbolic Law.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/thantiklermcirony/bounded-observer"
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Bounded Composition and Its Horizons: when a bounded quantity earns an additive chart, a horizon and a geometry"
    authors:
      - family-names: Murray
        given-names: Daniel John
    year: 2026
